--- Rosetta Code: Command-line arguments
--- https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Command-line_arguments
--- args[] is the list of the arguments written after the program, each as text,
--- the program's own name not among them. Run it with arguments as
---     crow run command_line_arguments.co -c "alpha beta" -h "gamma"
--- (crow run -i interprets it; crow build makes a program that takes them the
--- same way: ./command_line_arguments -c "alpha beta" -h "gamma").

given = args[]
log['number of arguments: `len[given]`']
log['args[] = `str[given]`']
for i in range[len[given]]
    log['argument `i + 1`: `given[i]`']
